<Template>
  <!--
    Description:
      One transparent tap target of the backdrop around the settings panel.
      Tapping it dismisses the panel, so BACK is a convenience rather than the
      only way out.
    Variables:
      Size: the area's size, as for any widget.

    The press is exactly the one SettingsBack makes: show_settings is 1 while
    the panel is open, so this toggle takes it to 0, and menu_disarm clears any
    armed confirm - a half-armed POWER OFF must never survive being tapped
    away, or reopening the menu would sit one tap from a shutdown.

    Four of these fence the panel in (above, below, left, right) rather than one
    full-screen button behind it. Fencing is what keeps the panel's own dead
    space inert: a tap on the panel background hits the panel group, which
    passes the event to its parent rather than to a sibling underneath, so
    missing a button by a few pixels never closes the menu.

    Unpatched Mixxx has no [Library],menu_disarm; the connection is ignored
    there and the dismissal still works, same as the rest of settings.xml.
  -->
  <PushButton>
    <ObjectName>SettingsScrimArea</ObjectName>
    <Size><Variable name="Size"/></Size>
    <NumberStates>2</NumberStates>
    <State>
      <Number>0</Number>
      <Text></Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>1</Number>
      <Text></Text>
    </State>
    <Connection>
      <ConfigKey persist="false">[Skin],show_settings</ConfigKey>
      <ButtonState>LeftButton</ButtonState>
    </Connection>
    <Connection>
      <ConfigKey persist="false">[Library],menu_disarm</ConfigKey>
      <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
      <EmitOnPressAndRelease>true</EmitOnPressAndRelease>
      <ButtonState>LeftButton</ButtonState>
    </Connection>
  </PushButton>
</Template>
